From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:36:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: model native Mac font-aware inline text dimensions

Replace the fixed five-pixel fallback for naturally sized leaf inline and
inline-block text boxes with deterministic, content-dependent dimensions.
Share the existing canvas font-family resolver and representative ASCII
advance tables through text_measure, preserving their attribution. Retain
Unicode/combining-character fallbacks and model whitespace, line breaks,
font-size scaling and line height without an installed macOS font backend.

Track copied text-style values through the existing stylesheet cascade and
invalidation machinery. Resolve inherited, relative and root-relative sizes,
font shorthand and all resets, and reject invalid supported longhands before
they replace valid declarations. Bound resolved sizes to keep hostile CSS
from producing non-finite geometry. Keep SVG presentation sizes and older
wrapping consumers connected to the same cascaded font-size resolution.

Expand and round-trip the supported font shorthand constituents through
native CSSOM bindings, retaining style/weight/variant/stretch even though the
synthetic measurement model does not shape them. Preserve mutation ordering
around all, including identical-value writes, and expose computed font sizes.

Keep explicit dimensions, hidden/zero-size boxes and existing block/replaced
layout paths intact. Bounding/client rectangles share fractional geometry;
integer client/offset/scroll dimensions round measured text boxes. This is
not full CSS layout, CoreText shaping, or transform support.

Update only existing StyleManager expectations for newly tracked display
values; add no permanent tests. Temporary fixtures passed 39 assertions.
Validation: scripts/build.sh; 1658/1658 upstream tests; unchanged benchmark
127/130 (97.69%), with dom-font-glyph-metrics now passing and no lost passes.
